 Remote pointing system used for targeting. Skyward Sword is structured very similar to previous Zelda games, as you travel through an overworld in search of temples to visit and once in you solve a series of puzzles before fighting a boss at the end and receive the next bit of plot. The biggest change is that the overworld is more focused on puzzles with only a handful of action.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}, {"id": 22, "name": "Historical"}, {"id": 38, "name": "Open world"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/the-legend-of-zelda-skyward-sword", "videos": [{"id": 19915, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "SMkvcKhVCEk", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SMkvcKhVCEk", "title": "Wii - The Legend of Zelda: Skyward Sword Trailer", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SMkvcKhVCEk/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 119513, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "Uz0Lia-HS8A", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Uz0Lia-HS8A", "title": "The Legend of Zelda: Skyward Sword (Wii) E3 2010 Trailer", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Uz0Lia-HS8A/hqdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 106, "name": "The Legend of Zelda"}]}